      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscoda%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 220‑mile Shore to Shore Riding & Hiking Trail ends its eastern stretch in Oscoda, linking the Great Lakes to the Upper Peninsula.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscoda%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Oscoda sits at the mouth of the Au Sable River where it empties into Lake Huron, straddling the river’s north side.",
